  "ph": "ph_opt = target range. ph_tol = outer limits; outside these expect real yield loss or nutrient lockup. Between opt and tol = 'marginal'.",
  "ec": "EC values are ECe (saturated-paste extract, dS/m) \u2014 the standard for crop salt-tolerance data. Maas-Hoffman: relative_yield% = 100 - slope*(ECe - threshold) when ECe > threshold.",
  "ec_source": {
   "MH": "Published threshold + slope (Maas & Hoffman 1977; Maas & Grattan 1999; FAO-29/USDA Salinity Lab tables)",
   "CLASS": "Only a qualitative rating is published; threshold set to the low edge of that class (S 1.0, MS 1.3, MT 3.0, T 6.0). Slope unknown.",
   "EST": "No published rating; estimated from the most similar crop. Treat as a placeholder."
  },
  "IMPORTANT_ec_units": "Convert your sensor reading to ECe before comparing. Rough factors (texture-dependent \u2014 calibrate with a few lab saturated-paste samples): ECe \u2248 2.0 \u00d7 EC(1:1 soil:water); ECe \u2248 6.4 \u00d7 EC(1:5). In-field probe bulk EC is NOT comparable without moisture correction.",
  "ph_sources": "Consensus extension ranges (Texas A&M AgriLife, NRCS, land-grant extension guides). ph_confidence='estimated' where the crop has little published guidance."
